{"chapter": "schemes", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "01KH", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$f : X \\to T$", "MATH_0002": "$g : Y \\to T$", "MATH_0003": "$h : T \\to S$", "MATH_0004": "$i : X \\times_T Y \\to X \\times_S Y$", "MATH_0005": "$T \\to S$", "MATH_0006": "$i$", "MATH_0007": "$T \\to S$", "MATH_0008": "$i$"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-fibre-product-after-map}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:31748520917783a2f119a2a83ce4d73eddc5f536d00d85824645998d1338418d", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:1807c8693d465928a964e9997b24494ca6c38a94c1273287e7be933147344761", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> and <MATH_0002> be morphisms of schemes\nwith the same target. Let <MATH_0003> be a morphism of schemes.\nThen the induced morphism <MATH_0004> is\nan immersion. If <MATH_0005> is separated, then <MATH_0006> is a closed\nimmersion. If <MATH_0007> is quasi-separated, then <MATH_0008> is a\nquasi-compact morphism.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:0254deb509421b7a474d423056b0ae8a8c0b3981ef8a2e107568ef6ac8090f30", "unit_id": "tag:01KR:statement"}
{"chapter": "schemes", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "01KH", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$$\n\\xymatrix{\nX \\times_T Y \\ar[r] \\ar[d] & X \\times_S Y \\ar[d] \\\\\nT \\ar[r]^{\\Delta_{T/S}} \\ar[r] & T \\times_S T\n}\n$$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{lemma-diagonal-immersion}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{lemma-fibre-product-immersion}", "REF_0003": "\\ref{lemma-quasi-compact-preserved-base-change}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:f5a6ec1e0e539ca3f309ad7354dab4e755c6e3b3d7bd2c73969a5dd5936eb17a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:ffabb35d056125ed71b261f5489ff529b21328e652edd06c054cc67d699cabaa", "source_text": "By general category theory the following diagram\n<MATH_0001>\nis a fibre product diagram. The lemma follows\nfrom Lemmas <REF_0001>,\n<REF_0002> and\n<REF_0003>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:302248cc888a8f725da04bae34ca936d2a0e04b3046c9a99953c318c709c8888", "unit_id": "tag:01KR:proof"}
{"chapter": "schemes", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "01KH", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$g : X \\to Y$", "MATH_0002": "$S$", "MATH_0003": "$i : X \\to X \\times_S Y$", "MATH_0004": "$Y$", "MATH_0005": "$S$", "MATH_0006": "$Y$", "MATH_0007": "$S$"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-semi-diagonal}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:9beb9af06d51f28841a4c2c9907219a825fc5e490b22cecba8f436586384b2e6", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:862ec2324f79363fed753c166d1a5c9ebc931e53d01e920f3738d52f02e9ba64", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a morphism of schemes over <MATH_0002>.\nThe morphism <MATH_0003> is an immersion.\nIf <MATH_0004> is separated over <MATH_0005> it is a closed immersion.\nIf <MATH_0006> is quasi-separated over <MATH_0007> it is quasi-compact.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:7c8f74535a57a6920f9d24708fc556fa04c9d0a925e4fcee7d2a67cbd2b47162", "unit_id": "tag:01KS:statement"}
{"chapter": "schemes", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "01KH", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$X = X \\times_Y Y \\to X \\times_S Y$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{lemma-fibre-product-after-map}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:70de829f83fe0a46b7049636ec5c0c1d48b0f22d74c8caea2ec31210b4337758", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:4280f2bfeb45432bb93a6d7b2adc26c3026bcfd4b0ae74a37d7c025812a0b5f3", "source_text": "This is a special case of Lemma <REF_0001>\napplied to the morphism <MATH_0001>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:93a713d4018ed194be2d6b2380b756e9479485f580e665efd59b7efdef2d736a", "unit_id": "tag:01KS:proof"}
{"chapter": "schemes", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "01KH", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$f : X \\to S$", "MATH_0002": "$s : S \\to X$", "MATH_0003": "$f$", "MATH_0004": "$f \\circ s = \\text{id}_S$", "MATH_0005": "$s$", "MATH_0006": "$f$", "MATH_0007": "$s$", "MATH_0008": "$f$", "MATH_0009": "$s$"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-section-immersion}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:6929bc64063e7601bb644c416e2007715714eda06c1f7785e1b7bd97522cb850", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:31532bee5bfb4640a4233e8f02b367723bb57cf90785de5c668fade96d0ada29", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a morphism of schemes.\nLet <MATH_0002> be a section of <MATH_0003> (in a formula <MATH_0004>).\nThen <MATH_0005> is an immersion.\nIf <MATH_0006> is separated then <MATH_0007> is a closed immersion.\nIf <MATH_0008> is quasi-separated, then <MATH_0009> is quasi-compact.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:eec13c10b1ff9ff15ee28a188b0ad2bbcb95890037a63a539e46bf7202ddca79", "unit_id": "tag:01KT:statement"}
{"chapter": "schemes", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "01KH", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$g =s$", "MATH_0002": "$i = s : S \\to S \\times_S X$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{lemma-semi-diagonal}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:39fd9ad136778db28afa2ffcfc076506e0b553ed85d73599ffae5951a4fbf3da", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:b3790cd0ae9f89fbb12a417e2bc7da14003de513ba1234b3c3448d9ce3009fb9", "source_text": "This is a special case of Lemma <REF_0001> applied to\n<MATH_0001> so the morphism <MATH_0002>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:4973fec130a03fca9689063f58cb57938908596e039918f8833593c6ffe1b375", "unit_id": "tag:01KT:proof"}
{"chapter": "schemes", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "01KH", "placeholders": {"STRUCT_0001": "\\begin{enumerate}", "STRUCT_0002": "\\item", "STRUCT_0003": "\\item", "STRUCT_0004": "\\item", "STRUCT_0005": "\\item", "STRUCT_0006": "\\item", "STRUCT_0007": "\\item", "STRUCT_0008": "\\end{enumerate}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-separated-permanence}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:42224d6825af2c451bbdd5c8672916d8dff6e63cd340fd4b966accee80e123da", "source_text": "Permanence properties.\n<STRUCT_0001>\n<STRUCT_0002> A composition of separated morphisms is separated.\n<STRUCT_0003> A composition of quasi-separated morphisms is quasi-separated.\n<STRUCT_0004> The base change of a separated morphism is separated.\n<STRUCT_0005> The base change of a quasi-separated morphism is quasi-separated.\n<STRUCT_0006> A (fibre) product of separated morphisms is separated.\n<STRUCT_0007> A (fibre) product of quasi-separated morphisms is quasi-separated.\n<STRUCT_0008>\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:e16647e2bbcf58d8da85f929e98c7bc75a7544e7892d675d02400ea536fb5825", "unit_id": "tag:01KU:statement"}
